endobj
147 0 obj
<</AP<</N 194 0 R >>/DA(/Helv 10 Tf 0 g)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/MK<<>>/P 15 0 R /Rect[ 108.348 52.9869 534.996 198.97]/Subtype/Widget/T(q6)/Type/Annot/V(The Windows Server Active Directory achieve the three elements of CIA \(Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability\), by admins able to choose which LANS, folders, and data are available for any users on the network, choosing their set privileges, and ability to setup privacy and password policies. With this directory, the administrator can restrict the information to only those who are allowed to view said information and who can tweak it. As well as choose which users are able to keep the information as secure and accurate as possible, to be the best usage of data. Lastly, the directory allows all data to be available to users who are authorized, and is able to keep all data easily accessible for those that are permitted, but protects from intruders. With this, the local networks, folders, and data that go to their respected departments are only accessed by authorized users only.)>>
endobj
