<</AP<</N 196 0 R >>/DA(/Helv 10 Tf 0 g)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/MK<<>>/P 17 0 R /Rect[ 109.049 513.932 535.697 660.839]/Subtype/Widget/T(q7)/Type/Annot/V(No, it is not a good idea whatsoever to include the user name or account in a password, as it makes the password that much more vulnerable and easily decoded, since it is possible to easily guess the password due to the user name or account publicly known. Passwords are not meant to be easily known nor known by more than one person, thus making one's password easier to decode puts a person's information at risk, as well as their peers and business possibly.)>>
